course: dictionary
lesson: 6819
title: Osiers and the river bank
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture of a place. Osier is one of them. When you meet it, look at the words around it to find out where the story is happening. «The Mole at first heard nothing but the wind playing in the reeds and rushes and osiers.» The list of reeds, rushes and osiers tells you this is a river bank, because all three grow in wet places.
explain: Osier is not the same as reed or rush. The sentence names all three separately, so they must be different plants. An osier is a kind of willow, with long thin bendy twigs. Reeds and rushes are tall grassy plants that grow in water.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Put in «willow» for osiers: «the wind playing in the reeds and rushes and willows». It still makes sense, so you have a good guess. A dictionary can confirm that osier means a willow with long thin bendy shoots.
fact: An osier is a kind of willow tree or bush.
fact: Osiers grow by rivers and on wet ground.
fact: One osier is a single long, thin, bendy willow shoot.
fact: Osiers are cut and woven into baskets, fences and fish traps.
fact: «An osier basket» is a basket woven from willow shoots. «Osier beds» are places where osiers are grown.
exercise: «The Mole heard the wind playing in the reeds and rushes and osiers.» What are osiers? | Small boats for rowing | Birds that sing at dawn | Fish that swim in rivers | *A kind of willow with long thin bendy twigs
exercise: Which thing is usually made from osier shoots? | A metal bucket | *A woven basket | A cup for drinking | A stone wall
exercise: Mira says osier is just a fancy word for reed. Why is she wrong? | Reeds grow on mountains and osiers grow in towns | Reeds are willows and osiers are grass | *The sentence lists reeds and osiers separately, so they are different plants | Osiers are a type of fish
test: What kind of place do reeds, rushes and osiers grow in? | *A wet place by a river | A hot desert | A snowy mountain | A busy town
test: Ben reads «an osier basket» and asks what it is made from. What is the answer? | Plastic strips | Straw from wheat | *Long thin bendy willow shoots | Tin
exam: An osier basket is made from what? | Straw from wheat | Tin | Plastic strips | *Long thin bendy willow shoots
